{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",

  // Dead-code gate for every workspace. knip resolves each workspace's entry points, then
  // reports everything under its `project` that no entry reaches, transitively. That is the
  // whole claim this file makes.
  //
  // RUN IT FROM THE WORKSPACE ROOT — `pnpm structure:dead-code` runs every workspace, and
  // `pnpm --filter @ai-sidekicks/desktop structure:dead-code` runs the desktop alone from here
  // via `--directory ../..`. The workspace keys below are therefore repo-root-relative. Running
  // from the workspace root is not a preference: a package-scoped run cannot see the
  // workspace-root `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, so every `catalog:` specifier reports unresolved, and
  // it cannot see the root manifest, so `tsc` / `eslint` / `turbo` report as unlisted
  // binaries. Both classes vanish here, and neither is silenced by an ignore entry.
  //
  // The root workspace is declared with empty globs on purpose: knip then reads its manifest
  // for dependency resolution while contributing no findings of its own.
  // The per-symbol dead-code lever. knip reads JSDoc/TSDoc tags off an export and
  // `-consumedBy` excludes every export carrying `@consumedBy` from the report — the
  // documented `tags` option, which is what `apps/desktop/AGENTS.md` binds to a plain-word
  // reason. It is per SYMBOL, unlike `ignore` (file globs) and `ignoreIssues` (issue types
  // per file pattern), neither of which is used here: exempting a file would exempt every
  // export it ever grows.
  //
  // The one per-FILE lever is `ignoreFiles`, for a whole file kept for a consumer that is
  // not built yet: one exact path per entry, never a directory or a glob, each with a
  // comment naming the design, plan or build unit that owns it. The entry leaves in the
  // change that builds its consumer. It clears only the file it names, so a chain of
  // unwired files takes one entry per file.
  //
  // MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED — the tag sits on every place knip reports. For a barrelled
  // symbol that is the barrel's own re-export specifier: knip reads per-specifier tags on
  // an `export { … } from` (its `handleExportNamed`). When the barrel is the defining
  // file's ONLY importer, knip reports the defining declaration as well, so that
  // declaration carries the tag too. A tag anywhere knip does not report suppresses
  // nothing and raises an "unused tag" hint, and `--treat-tag-hints-as-errors` turns that
  // hint into a gate failure, so a marker that outlived its consumer fails the run
  // instead of rotting: the PR that imports the symbol deletes the tag in the same diff.
  "tags": ["-consumedBy"],

  "workspaces": {
    ".": {
      "entry": [],
      "project": [],
      // `semver` is required by the CI workflow's inline `node -e` scripts, which knip does not
      // read.
      "ignoreDependencies": ["semver"]
    },

    "apps/desktop": {
      // NO `entry` DECLARATION, deliberately. knip's defaults already cover the three process
      // entries (`src/main/index.ts`, `src/preload/index.ts`, `src/renderer/src/main.tsx`) and
      // the two tool configs (`vitest.config.ts`, `electron.vite.config.ts`), and knip resolves
      // the rest from this package's own manifest: a file named in a `scripts` entry is an
      // entry, so `build/assert-webprefs.ts` and both `scripts/budget/measure-*.mts` are roots
      // because the `build`, `budget:bundle`, and `budget:heap` scripts run them. Measured, not
      // assumed — dropping the globs moved no file into `Unused files`.
      //
      // Declaring `scripts/**` as an entry glob instead would be actively worse: every helper
      // under it becomes a root, so a dead export in `scripts/budget/budget-registry.mts` — a
      // module nothing invokes by name — would be exempt rather than reported. It was, until
      // this glob was removed; a planted export there is now caught.
      //
      // Listing the defaults again is drift the run refuses: `--treat-config-hints-as-errors`
      // fails the gate on a redundant or unmatched pattern.

      // `project` is the universe the entry set is measured against. `build/**` runs during
      // `pnpm build`; `scripts/**` is invoked by name from a package script. Both trees are
      // TypeScript today; the `.mjs` / `.cjs` arms stay anyway, because `apps/desktop/AGENTS.md`
      // binds the TypeScript posture as a rule a reader follows, and a glob that could not see
      // a JavaScript file would let one escape the gate silently rather than report it. A brace
      // pattern is hinted on the whole pattern rather than per arm, so an arm matching nothing
      // today costs nothing under `--treat-config-hints-as-errors`.

      // The renderer's compile-time icon resolver is declared in `vitest/icon-compilation.ts`
      // and installed by BOTH `vitest.config.ts` and `electron.vite.config.ts`, which are
      // knip entries. Without `vitest/**` in the universe those two entries reach a file knip
      // does not analyse, so `unplugin-icons` and `@svgr/core` — imported there and nowhere
      // else — reported as unused dependencies. Measured: adding this glob cleared both and
      // moved no other file into any report.
      "project": [
        "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
        "fixtures/**/*.ts",
        "build/**/*.{ts,mts,mjs,cjs}",
        "scripts/**/*.{ts,mts,mjs,cjs}",
        "tests/**/*.{ts,tsx}",
        "vitest/**/*.ts"
      ],

      // The first-party `unplugin-icons` plugin, named rather than left to knip's own
      // enabler check, because what it does is not guessable from the manifest: it excuses
      // `~icons/*` specifiers from the unresolved report and `@iconify-json/*` from the
      // dependency one. The icon SETS are reached only through those virtual specifiers, so
      // without the plugin `@iconify-json/tabler` is an unused dependency that is in fact
      // the source of eleven of the renderer's thirty-six glyphs — and the only other way to
      // say so would be an `ignoreDependencies` entry, which `apps/desktop/AGENTS.md` admits
      // none of.
      "unplugin-icons": true,

      // The Vitest plugin reads the config and treats every project's `include` globs as
      // entries, so a test file is a root and what it imports is reached. Without it every
      // test file reports as an unused file and every test-only export as unused.
      //
      // WHICH IS ALSO THIS GATE'S ONE BLIND SPOT, and it is a property of the entry set
      // rather than of anything declared here. An entry that reaches a DIRECTORY — a
      // renderer suite written `import.meta.glob("../**/*.{ts,tsx}", { query: "?raw" })`,
      // which Vite resolves at transform time and the plugin above reads as one edge per
      // matched file — makes every module under that directory reachable, so no orphan
      // below it can be reported. Measured 2026-09-08: a wholly unreachable module planted
      // at `src/renderer/src/lib/` was reported by nothing at rc 0, while the same
      // plant under `scripts/budget/` failed the run at rc 1. No setting here can see that
      // — the edge is real and the entry is one this plugin is right to claim — so the rule
      // lives where the pattern is written: the test rules in `apps/desktop/AGENTS.md` forbid a
      // directory glob in any module under `src/`, and `no-restricted-syntax` in
      // `apps/desktop/eslint.config.mjs` enforces it.
      "vitest": { "config": ["vitest.config.ts"] },

      // A same-file consumer counts as a consumer. Without this, every helper a module uses
      // internally and also exports for its own co-located test reports as an unused export.
      "ignoreExportsUsedInFile": true,

      // `xdpyinfo` is an X11 host utility the Xvfb smoke helper probes with `spawnSync` on
      // Linux runners (`tests/helpers/display-readiness.ts`); it is installed by the CI job's apt
      // step and is never a package dependency, so knip is told not to expect it in a manifest.
      "ignoreBinaries": ["xdpyinfo"],

      // Whole files kept for a consumer that is not built yet, each with its owner.
      "ignoreFiles": [
        // Scripted diff patches kept as the fixtures' test data (register WT-14); the diff read
        // that plays them is built with the Review pane (build units DM-16 and B9).
        "fixtures/data/repos-diff-patches.ts",
        // The anchored popover that registers its airspace over the Preview page: the
        // worktree popover and the context ring's compaction popover (session design S-125,
        // S-312, S-890).
        "src/renderer/src/components/OverlayPopups/OverlayPopoverPopup.tsx",
        // The row that offers wire identifiers to choose between: the sessions list (build
        // units A6 to A13) and the Workflows scope picker.
        "src/renderer/src/components/WireChoiceList/WireChoiceList.tsx",
        // The agent library's chunk, mounted by the Sidekicks screen's registration (build
        // unit K4).
        "src/renderer/src/features/agents/library/agent-library-body.ts",
        // An approval card takes focus when it arrives (session design S-727; build unit B7).
        "src/renderer/src/features/composer/approval/hooks/useApprovalArrivalAnnouncement.ts",
        // An agent's question card and the settlement it reads (session design D-66; build
        // unit B8).
        "src/renderer/src/features/composer/question-card/BoundQuestionCard.tsx",
        "src/renderer/src/store/session-events/hooks/useQuestionSettlement.ts",
        // Interrupt and Interrupt everything on the run controls (session design S-105 to
        // S-108; build units A14 and B13).
        "src/renderer/src/features/composer/run-controls/hooks/useRunDriverBindings.ts",
        // The cost receipt's partition rule, which becomes a daemon test on the receipt fold
        // (register AGT-7; the inspector's Cost section, session design S-324); the entry
        // leaves with the rest of the file.
        "src/renderer/src/features/inspector/cost/cost-receipt-model.ts",
        // The inspector's Rules section with Revoke (session design S-971; build units B10
        // and DM-18).
        "src/renderer/src/features/inspector/rules/components/RulesSection.tsx",
        // The session header's title read and its fixture answer (session design S-046,
        // S-305; build units A9 and DM-19).
        "src/renderer/src/features/sessions/session-header/hooks/useSessionHeaderRead.ts",
        "src/renderer/src/features/sessions/session-header/hooks/useSessionIdentity.ts",
        "src/renderer/src/services/daemon/session-identity.fixture.ts",
        "src/renderer/src/services/daemon/session-reads.ts",
        // The operating-system notification permission fold, which moves to main beside the
        // notification poster (registers SH-09 and ATT-1; build unit B14).
        "src/renderer/src/features/settings/pages/notifications/os-notification-delivery.ts",
        // A footnote's definition at the foot of its reply (session design S-657; build unit
        // A20).
        "src/renderer/src/features/transcript/rows/markdown/footnotes/DefinitionBody.tsx",
        // A run's page refreshing live (build unit WF-15).
        "src/renderer/src/features/workflows/run-page/hooks/useWorkflowRunLiveRefresh.ts"
      ]
    },

    // The packages declare no source `entry`: knip reads each one's entries from its own
    // manifest (`exports`, whose `@ai-sidekicks/source` condition points at `src/`), and its
    // plugins add the rest — every package's `vitest.config.ts` test files, and the control
    // plane's worker entry from `wrangler.toml`. Each ignore below names a dependency knip
    // cannot see being used, with the reason.
    "packages/contracts": {
      // The conditional-type tests beside the contracts; `tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` checks
      // them, and nothing imports them.
      "entry": ["src/**/*.test-d.ts"]
    },
    "packages/crypto-paseto": {},
    "packages/search-ranking": {},
    "packages/client-sdk": {},
    "packages/control-plane": {
      // The Cloudflare CLI: the worker is run with `wrangler dev` and published with
      // `wrangler deploy` by hand, so no package script names it. `pg` and its types are the
      // Postgres client the control plane's stores are built on, not imported until those
      // stores land.
      // `@ai-sidekicks/contracts` is imported only by the ignored file below.
      "ignoreDependencies": ["wrangler", "pg", "@types/pg", "@ai-sidekicks/contracts"],
      // The roster's per-shell reading of the terminal write lease holder, which nothing
      // imports until the roster joins the persisted holder.
      "ignoreFiles": ["src/runtime-nodes/attach-service.ts"]
    },
    "packages/runtime-daemon": {
      // Loaded by `import()` of a specifier held in a variable (`pty/node-pty-host.ts`), which
      // knip cannot follow; it is a hard runtime dependency.
      "ignoreDependencies": ["node-pty"]
    }
  }
}
